IX["EHSAN-ANAT-TRIGEMINAL-5TH-CRANIAL-NERVE-MCQ-"] = Object.assign(IX["EHSAN-ANAT-TRIGEMINAL-5TH-CRANIAL-NERVE-MCQ-"] || {}, {
  1: ["The **mylohyoid** is supplied by the nerve to mylohyoid (inferior alveolar → **posterior** division).", "a: Buccinator: facial.", "c: Stylohyoid: facial.", "d: Posterior belly of digastric: facial."],
  10: ["The **lesser palatine** nerves come off the sphenopalatine (pterygopalatine) ganglion to the soft palate.", "a: The greater superficial petrosal is the ganglion's **parasympathetic root**, not its branch.", "b: The lesser petrosal goes to the **otic** ganglion.", "c: The auricular branch belongs to the vagus."],
  13: ["The **superior** alveolar nerves are branches of the **maxillary** nerve, not the mandibular.", "a: True: the nerve to medial pterygoid comes from the trunk.", "c: True: the inferior alveolar is from the posterior division.", "d: True: the auriculotemporal is from the posterior division."],
  14: ["Deep facial and nasal pain between the mouth and the orbit is carried by the **maxillary** nerve (V2: cheek, upper jaw, nose, palate).", "a: The ophthalmic serves the forehead, eye and upper nose.", "c: 'Hypopharyngeal nerve' is not a nerve of the face.", "d: The facial nerve is motor to the face (sensory only for taste and a small ear area)."],
  15: ["The maxillary nerve leaves the skull through the **foramen rotundum** into the pterygopalatine fossa.", "a: The foramen ovale transmits V3.", "b: The sphenopalatine foramen joins the pterygopalatine fossa to the nose.", "c: The foramen spinosum transmits the middle meningeal artery."],
  20: ["Taste from the anterior 2/3: **chorda tympani** (facial nerve).", "b: The lingual carries **general** sensation (the chorda's fibres only ride with it).", "c: The internal laryngeal serves the epiglottic region.", "d: The hypoglossal is motor.", "e: The glossopharyngeal serves the posterior 1/3."],
  26: ["Pain from the anterior 2/3 of the tongue travels in the **lingual** nerve.", "b: The hypoglossal is motor.", "c: The glossopharyngeal serves the posterior 1/3.", "d: The vagus serves the root near the epiglottis."],
  29: ["The inferior alveolar gives the **nerve to mylohyoid** → **mylohyoid** (and anterior digastric).", "b: Geniohyoid: C1.", "c: Hyoglossus: hypoglossal.", "d: Stylohyoid: facial."],
  30: ["Injury at the origin of the inferior alveolar nerve cuts the nerve to mylohyoid → paralysis of the **anterior belly of digastric** (and mylohyoid).", "a: Stylohyoid: facial.", "b: Posterior belly of digastric: facial.", "c: Geniohyoid: C1."],
  31: ["Taste from the anterior 2/3 is the **7th (facial)** nerve.", "a: The 5th carries general sensation.", "b: The 6th is motor to the lateral rectus.", "d: The 9th carries taste from the posterior 1/3."],
});

IX["EHSAN-ANAT-MAXILLARY-ARTERY-PTERYGOID-VENOUS-PLEXUS-MCQ-"] = Object.assign(IX["EHSAN-ANAT-MAXILLARY-ARTERY-PTERYGOID-VENOUS-PLEXUS-MCQ-"] || {}, {
  3: ["The **accessory meningeal** artery is a **1st-part** branch (with the middle meningeal, deep auricular, anterior tympanic, inferior alveolar).", "a: The sphenopalatine is 3rd part.", "b: The greater palatine is 3rd part.", "d: The buccal is 2nd part."],
  7: ["The middle meningeal vessels enter the skull through the **foramen spinosum**.", "a: The foramen ovale transmits V3 (and the accessory meningeal artery).", "c: The foramen lacerum is closed by cartilage.", "d: The foramen rotundum transmits V2."],
  9: ["The middle meningeal artery is a branch of the **maxillary** artery (1st part).", "a: Not the internal carotid.", "b: Not the middle cerebral.", "d: The deep temporal arteries are its sister branches (2nd part)."],
});

IX["EHSAN-ANAT-CRANIAL-CAVITY-MCQ-"] = Object.assign(IX["EHSAN-ANAT-CRANIAL-CAVITY-MCQ-"] || {}, {
  2: ["The **inner (meningeal) layer** of the dura folds inward (falx, tentorium) to separate parts of the brain.", "b: The extradural space is between the dura and the **bone**.", "c: The **pia** dips into the sulci; the arachnoid bridges them.", "d: CSF is in the **subarachnoid** space."],
  5: ["The **trochlear** nerve is embedded in the lateral wall of the cavernous sinus.", "a: The facial nerve goes into the internal acoustic meatus.", "c: The mandibular division does not touch the sinus.", "d: The olfactory nerve is in the anterior fossa."],
  8: ["The **ophthalmic** division runs in the lateral wall of the cavernous sinus.", "a: The internal carotid runs **forward** through the sinus and leaves through its roof.", "b: The abducent lies **lateral** (inferolateral) to the internal carotid.", "d: The maxillary division is in the **lateral wall** (lower part), not the roof."],
  11: ["The **inferior petrosal** sinuses are **paired** (one each side).", "a: The superior sagittal is single (midline).", "b: The straight sinus is single.", "c: The occipital sinus is single."],
  12: ["The **abducent** nerve lies free inside the sinus right next to the internal carotid, so an ICA aneurysm there hits it **first** (lateral rectus palsy).", "b: The oculomotor is protected in the lateral wall.", "c: The ophthalmic is in the lateral wall.", "d: The maxillary is in the lower lateral wall."],
  13: ["The **mandibular** division is not in the cavernous sinus wall.", "a: Oculomotor: lateral wall.", "b: Trochlear: lateral wall.", "c: Ophthalmic: lateral wall."],
  16: ["The **superior ophthalmic vein** (from the angular/facial vein) drains straight into the cavernous sinus — the most direct route.", "a: The pterygoid plexus is an indirect route (deep facial vein → emissary veins).", "c: The frontal plexus is not the main route.", "d: The parietal emissary vein links the scalp to the superior sagittal sinus."],
  22: ["False: the **inferior sagittal** sinus is in the falx's free border; the **straight** sinus runs along its junction with the tentorium.", "a: True: it is attached behind to the upper surface of the tentorium.", "c: True: it is attached in front to the crista galli and frontal crest.", "d: True: it lies between the medial surfaces of the hemispheres."],
});

IX["EHSAN-ANAT-ORBIT-MCQ-"] = Object.assign(IX["EHSAN-ANAT-ORBIT-MCQ-"] || {}, {
  1: ["The **central artery of the retina** is a branch of the **ophthalmic** artery.", "b: It enters the optic nerve on its **inferomedial** side.", "c: Its branches **are end arteries** (occlusion → sudden blindness).", "d: It gives no branches to extraocular muscles."],
  4: ["Eye down and out + complete ptosis + dilated pupil = **oculomotor nerve** palsy (e.g. compressed by a tumour).", "a: Optic nerve damage causes blindness, not a squint.", "b: The facial nerve closes the eye; it does not lift the lid.", "c: A ciliary ganglion lesion affects only the pupil and accommodation."],
  10: ["Looking left needs the **left lateral rectus**; its failure gives an inward (convergent) squint → **abducent** nerve injury.", "a: The nasociliary is sensory.", "c: The trochlear supplies the superior oblique.", "d: The superior division of III supplies superior rectus and levator."],
  12: ["The smooth-muscle part of **levator palpebrae superioris** (Müller's superior tarsal muscle) is sympathetic; its paralysis gives partial ptosis (Horner's syndrome).", "a: Superior rectus has no smooth part.", "b: Superior oblique has no smooth part.", "d: Depressor anguli oris is a facial muscle of the mouth."],
});

